description:
Producer half of task-e3e81c45 (HIGH). There, a UnAI seat's Serena server is unusable for 15-23 min at startup, because Serena's startup .gitignore walk ignores .git/info/exclude and walks 112 excluded worktrees. Split by architect-24611a0a on 2026-11-03: the parent keeps the human DoD, wires both launchers to this script, and lands last.

OBJECTIVE
A standalone Node script (node: builtins only). For one Serena project root, it writes a Moe-managed block into <root>/.serena/project.local.yml that turns Serena's startup walk off (`ignore_all_files_in_gitignore: false`). It hands Serena the same patterns that walk would have built, plus the ones git honours and Serena does not.

Background (serena-agent 1.6.2):
- Serena applies project.local.yml as a shallow key override over project.yml (serena/config/serena_config.py ~:713, yaml_data.update).
- Its ignore spec is ignored_paths plus, only when the flag is true, a breadth-first .gitignore walk (serena/util/file_system.py GitignoreParser).
- The patterns are gitwildmatch, and the last match wins.

DELIVERABLE
1. scripts/moe-serena-ignore.mjs. Usage: `node moe-serena-ignore.mjs <serena-root>`. It always exits 0 and prints exactly one of these lines:
   - `[OK] MOE_SERENA_IGNORE_OVERRIDE: wrote <file> (<n> patterns; Serena's .gitignore walk is off)`
   - `[info] MOE_SERENA_IGNORE_OVERRIDE: <file> is up to date (<n> patterns)`
   - `[info] MOE_SERENA_IGNORE_SKIPPED: <reason>; Serena keeps its own .gitignore walk`
2. Patterns, in this order (Serena's own order):
   - "/.git";
   - project.yml's own ignored_paths, verbatim (a local key replaces the project's);
   - then the lines of core.excludesFile (`git config --path --get core.excludesFile`, else $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/git/ignore or ~/.config/git/ignore), info/exclude (`git rev-parse --git-path info/exclude`), and each .gitignore that `git ls-files -z --cached --others --exclude-standard -- ':(glob)**/.gitignore'` lists (parents before children).
   Each line is converted exactly as Serena's GitignoreParser._parse_gitignore_content converts it:
   - rstrip; blank and comment lines dropped;
   - '!' kept;
   - a leading '\#' or '\!' unescaped;
   - a leading '/' anchors;
   - a nested file's unanchored pattern becomes <dir>/**/<pattern> (<dir>/<pattern> if it starts with '**/'), and its anchored one <dir>/<pattern>;
   - info/exclude and core.excludesFile count as root-level files.
3. The block, in this order:
   - a begin marker line;
   - comment lines saying why (Serena's walk ignores .git/info/exclude and core.excludesFile) and how to opt out;
   - `ignore_all_files_in_gitignore: false`;
   - `ignored_paths:` with one `- <JSON-quoted string>` per pattern;
   - an end marker line.
   Everything outside the block is the user's and is kept byte-for-byte. A previous block is replaced, never duplicated. The file is written only when its bytes change: LF, UTF-8 without BOM, through a temp file in .serena/ and a rename.
4. Opt-outs, which leave Serena's defaults: MOE_SERENA_IGNORE_OVERRIDE=0, or a user part that sets ignore_all_files_in_gitignore or ignored_paths at top level. Both remove a previous Moe block (so no key is ever duplicated) and write nothing else.
5. Fail-open skips, which change nothing:
   - the root is not a git work tree, or not its top level;
   - a git call fails or takes over 20 s;
   - under MOE_RUNTIME_PROTECTED=1, MOE_PROTECTED_GIT is not an absolute path (task-3acf7f79 exports it; never spawn a bare-name git under the marker);
   - git does not ignore .serena/project.local.yml (`git check-ignore -q`; this also covers a tracked file), or the file is not a regular file;
   - a begin marker without its end;
   - project.yml's ignored_paths is not a block or flow sequence of plain or quoted scalars;
   - the root has a submodule (an index gitlink) or an untracked, unignored nested repository (Serena's walk reads their .gitignore files; git's listing does not);
   - more than 5000 patterns.
6. scripts/tests/serena-ignore.test.mjs (node:test), plus a scripts/bundle-manifest.json `files` entry, so both IDE plugins ship the script next to the wrappers.

NOT IN SCOPE
- Calling the script from moe-agent.{sh,ps1}, the launch-level tests and the docs: all task-e3e81c45.
- Any change to Serena itself.

VERIFICATION
`node --test scripts/tests/serena-ignore.test.mjs` on Linux and through Windows node.exe (from a normal WSL shell), then `npm run lint`.
